# Build context exclusions for the site image.
# Dockerfile: deploy/Dockerfile.site, context: repository root.
#
# Two reasons this file matters:
#   1. `COPY . .` runs AFTER `npm ci`, so a host node_modules would overwrite the
#      modules npm just installed for the *container's* platform. Production is
#      linux/arm64 (Hetzner CAX), so x86 host binaries there break the build.
#   2. Without it, .env files, the CMS database and the git history are copied
#      into builder layers.

# Version control + CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.worktrees

# Installed + generated locally
node_modules
dist
test-results
playwright-report
*.tsbuildinfo

# Agent tooling, tests and documentation: not part of the shipped artifact.
.agents
docs
e2e
playwright.config.ts

# The CMS is its own build context (cms/) — never needed in the site image.
cms

# Secrets must never reach an image layer.
.env
.env.*
deploy/.env
deploy/.env.*
